	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="lt">Poilsis, kultūra ir religija</prefLabel>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="sk">Rekreácia, kultúra a náboženstvo</prefLabel>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="de">Freizeitgestaltung, Kultur und Religion</prefLabel>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="el">Ψυχαγωγία, πολιτισμός και θρησκεία</prefLabel>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="lv">Atpūta, kultūra un reliģija</prefLabel>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="bg">Развлечения, култура и религия</prefLabel>
	<identifier xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">08</identifier>
	<topConceptOf xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/7yx/cofog"/>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Government outlays on recreation, culture and religion include expenditures on services provided to individual persons and households and expenditures on services provided on a collective basis. Individual expenditures are allocated to groups (08.1) and (08.2); expenditures on collective services are assigned to groups (08.3) to (08.6).
Collective services are provided to the community as a whole. They include activities such as formulation and administration of government policy; formulation and enforcement of legislation and standards for providing recreational and cultural services; and applied research and experimental development into recreational, cultural and religious affairs and services.</definition>
</rdf:Description>

